// G3 grammar fixture for docs/prds/v0_6/angle-units-surface-convergence.md cluster B
// (ratified decision 6: hand-declared `Nm` torque unit symbol).
//
// THIS FIXTURE PARSES TODAY. Measured at HEAD dc83d4fd60:
// `tree-sitter parse --quiet` exits 0 — `Nm` is an ordinary `immediate_identifier`
// (grammar.js:1535, `/[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*/`) in the `unit_expr` suffix position.
// grammar_confirmed: TRUE — no grammar work is needed for the Nm cluster.
//
// What is NOT there yet is the unit-TABLE entry: `reify eval` on `5Nm` today says
// `error: unknown unit: Nm`. `Nm` exists in no .ri, no Rust table, and is not
// generated (si_units.rs only concatenates <prefix><name>; `N`'s prefix set is
// Only(["k","M","G"]) at si_units.rs:184). Producer: this PRD's leaf θ.
//
// Case-distinctness from `nm` (nanometre, GENERATED by si_units.rs:102-106 × the
// ("n", 1e-9) prefix at :22) is a property of the existing exact-HashMap lookup
// (reify-compiler/src/units.rs:1533 — zero case folding). Probe-verified today:
//   5nm -> 0.000000005 m      5Mm -> 5000000 m
//   5NM / 5MM / 5Kg / 5RAD -> error: unknown unit
// Leaf θ PINS that distinctness with a test rather than building it.
//
// `Torque` resolves today only via the stdlib alias
// `pub type Torque = Force * Length / Angle` (stdlib/ports_mechanical.ri:29), whose
// own header (:9-11) records that it exists *because* Torque is absent from
// NAMED_DIMENSIONS and because `unit` declarations take a named dimension, never a
// compound expression. Leaf η promotes Torque to a named dimension and retires the
// alias; θ then declares `pub unit Nm : Torque = 1`.
//
// Expected after θ: `5Nm` evaluates identically to `5N*m/rad`, and `5nm` still
// evaluates to 5e-9 m.

structure def UnitNmTorqueImmediate {
    let torque_compact  = 5Nm
    let torque_explicit = 5N*m/rad
    let nano_length     = 5nm
}
